{
  "overview": "This UX specification defines the complete user experience architecture for FSHQ.gg, a fantasy sports clubhouse platform. The design supports three primary user roles (Admin, Manager, Fan) with distinct permission levels and specialized workflows. The architecture centers around five core user journeys: (1) League Connection from Sleeper API with real-time sync validation, (2) Team Claiming with identity verification, (3) Commissioner Content Creation with draft/publish workflows and autosave, (4) Pick'ems Competition with lock-time enforcement and automated grading, and (5) Social Engagement through comments and reactions on feed moments. The UI follows a mobile-first responsive design approach with state-driven component patterns derived from application state machines. All interfaces support real-time updates via Supabase subscriptions, optimistic UI updates with rollback on error, and comprehensive error recovery procedures. The design system emphasizes accessibility (WCAG 2.1 AA), performance (sub-3s initial load, sub-500ms transitions), and progressive enhancement for offline capability.",

